# Formal verification of the von Neumann debiaser.
#
#   bmc    bounded model check: no input sequence of up to `depth` cycles from
#          reset can violate any property. The debiaser's state machine has a
#          period of two input samples, so 40 cycles covers every pairing,
#          alignment and discard case many times over.
#   cover  proves the properties are not vacuous: the solver must exhibit an
#          output of 0, an output of 1, and both discard cases.
#
# Not `mode prove`. k-induction hangs here, and the cause is the solver rather
# than the design: z3 4.8.12, which is what this machine has, does not converge
# on the induction step even after flattening, while the identical property
# written inside a single module proves by induction in one second. Newer solvers
# are not available in this environment (yices2 is not packaged, boolector is the
# 2012 1.5 release, cvc5 would not install). Recorded rather than papered over:
# what is claimed below is a bounded proof, not an unbounded one.
[tasks]
bmc
cover

[options]
bmc: mode bmc
bmc: depth 40
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 12

[engines]
smtbmc --nopresat z3

[script]
read -formal von_neumann.v
read -formal von_neumann_fv.v
prep -top von_neumann_fv -flatten

[files]
../src/von_neumann.v
von_neumann_fv.v
